
;; THE PROBE FOR `ropefind`. The cases are chosen for what a leaf walk can get
;; wrong and a flat search cannot:
;;
;;   SHAPE INDEPENDENCE. The same bytes as one flat leaf, as three leaves, and
;;     with an inline leaf in the middle, must all answer the same index.
;;   A MATCH ACROSS A BOUNDARY. `cab` inside [ab][ca][bc] exists only if the
;;     match continues into the next leaf, which is the case a per-leaf search
;;     misses entirely.
;;   A FAILED MATCH RESUMING. A candidate that matches two bytes and then
;;     fails must resume at the NEXT byte, not after the failed run -- the
;;     duplicate cursor is what makes that possible and what a bug here breaks.
;;   CODE POINTS, NOT BYTES. A two-byte character before the match shifts the
;;     byte offset and not the answer.
;;   FLATTENS = 0 for every haystack. This is the claim of the whole source,
;;     so the probe counts materialisations and prints the count.
